bar-lookup           14,571     14,777          -          -      1.01x           -   pk - already indexed by the primary key
bar-range             1,406      1,412          -          -      1.00x           -   pk - already indexed by the primary key
day-slice               411        414      8,870        411      1.01x      21.45x   daily_stats.session_no
symbol-history           33         32         34         32      0.97x       1.05x   daily_stats.symbol_id
cross-join              368        381      4,607        387      1.03x      12.10x   daily_stats.session_no
point-join            6,976      7,071          -          -      1.01x           -   pk - already indexed by the primary key
model-join            1,071      1,086      1,134      1,112      1.01x       1.04x   model_results.model_id

  symbol-history: cold ran 8 of 100 - the shape has fewer distinct arguments than that, and repeating one would have made it a warm case
  model-join: cold ran 8 of 100 - the shape has fewer distinct arguments than that, and repeating one would have made it a warm case

  cold    every argument seen for the first time: nothing of it is in
          shared_buffers or the OS page cache.
  warm    the same few arguments cycled. warm/cold is what repetition
          alone buys - here, almost entirely the buffer cache.
  index   warm, with a btree index on the filter column, created at
          runtime and ANALYZEd. It is `-` where the filter is the
          primary key, which already has one - the same reason the
          ckdbs side prints `-` there for a Cabin.
  dropped warm again straight after DROP INDEX, which is what makes
          the third column an isolated measurement of the index and
          not of whatever else warmed up while it existed.

